menu "Boca a Oreja listener"

    config BAO_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID"
        default "BAO-TEST"
        help
            The hub's access point, as set up by hub/setup-ap.sh.

    config BAO_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default "boca-a-oreja"

    config BAO_SERVER_IP
        string "Hub IP address"
        default "10.42.0.1"
        help
            Where hub/loadgen.py runs. 10.42.0.1 is the address NetworkManager gives
            the hub in a shared-mode access point, which is what setup-ap.sh creates.

    config BAO_SERVER_PORT
        int "Hub UDP port"
        default 5000

    config BAO_REPORT_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Report interval (ms)"
        default 2000

    config BAO_LATE_MS
        int "Late threshold (ms)"
        default 60
        help
            A packet delayed more than this beyond the recent minimum counts as late,
            i.e. it would have missed its slot in a typical playout buffer.

    config BAO_WIFI_POWER_SAVE
        bool "Use Wi-Fi power save (like a phone)"
        default y
        help
            Phones listening with the screen off use power save, which makes the AP
            buffer their frames between beacons and adds delay. Leave on for a
            realistic test; turn off to measure the radio on its own.

endmenu
